But why should we want to support different charactersets? Why not
simply support one characterset (like we do now) which is a little
larger than the one in use today? Why not unicode (16 bit) or its
successor ISO-whatever (I've forgotten the number) (32 bit)? This
approach offers the best of two worlds, as far as I can see. It
allows the use of non-american-English characters and it still
retains the advantages of having exactly one charset only (thus
avoiding possible ambiguities).

Cheers,
        Mike.

